{
  "id": "ticket_01KZ21KA4B0ZW32HXR12H1RHQE",
  "name": "Auto-compact events into a per-ticket archive on terminal transitions",
  "slug": "auto-compact-events-into-a",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "On done/drop, fold a ticket's loose event files into one archival record with full event fidelity. One-file-per-event stays for LIVE tickets (conflict-free parallel appends); after close it is pure overhead. Design AFTER event-cursors lands — same read paths and cursor semantics.",
    "details_md": "Requirements: reads transparently merge archive + residual loose events (cross-clone close-vs-append races); idempotent re-compaction via reindex; events --since and the poll-cursor protocol treat archived events identically; implemented in the flatfile driver behind StorageBackend. Helps t-407xr (show/search full-log scans). Ryan's original framing: compact on close or status change unless individual files have a benefit — they do for live tickets (merge-cleanliness, lock-free progress), hence terminal-transition-only.",
    "acceptance": [
      "Closing a ticket compacts its events; reads and cursors indistinguishable before/after",
      "Cross-clone merge of a close plus concurrent append reconciles without loss"
    ],
